  "ai": {
    "status": "ok",
    "model": "deepseek-chat",
    "summary": "The candidate change sets Deployment/demo/demo env[6] to DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL=true, which the FAULT_INJECTION rule blocks. Trusted cases confirm this value is a deliberate startup-failure drill: the new Pod logs startup_failed and enters CrashLoop while the old Pod stays Ready, so it validates rollout protection rather than a real outage. It must not be merged as a release. The decision preview is BLOCK and I do not override it. Secondary review items: 35 scheduled Pods lack CPU/memory requests, so free capacity (2190m CPU, ~9.2GB memory on one ready worker) may be overstated, and KubeCPUOvercommit is firing. Note the drill's maxUnavailable: 0 / maxSurge: 1 means capacity checks must count the retained old Pod plus the surge Pod.",
